Add Google Ads keyword, search term, device, and location reporting

AUDIT_REPORT.md flagged this as missing (High). New GAQL-based fetchers
(google-ads-breakdowns.ts) and orchestration layer
(google-ads-breakdowns-live.ts) mirror the Meta breakdown work — same
cache/multi-connection-merge/partial-failure pattern, reusing
google-ads-live.ts's resolveCreds (including its access-token refresh,
unlike Meta's pure-decrypt version) and a new shared mapGoogleAdsFacts
helper extracted from google-ads.ts's existing mapMetricsRow. Wired into
the shared AdsReport component as four new tables — Keywords, Search
terms, Device, Location — gated to provider === "google_ads" in live
mode.

Keywords and search terms are capped to the top 50 by spend directly in
the GAQL query (ORDER BY + LIMIT) rather than paginating everything —
this Google Ads client has never run against a real large account, so an
unbounded paginate-everything loop over what can be a very high-
cardinality report is a real risk, not a hypothetical one.

The location breakdown resolves Google's numeric geo target criterion
IDs to country codes via a small, hand-verified lookup table (cross-
checked against Google's published geo targets reference, not guessed)
covering major markets; an unmapped ID still shows up labeled by its raw
ID rather than being dropped or mislabeled — a wrong static ID-to-country
mapping would silently corrupt a client's location data with nothing to
catch it, so the table only includes entries actually confirmed.

